cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "BreedingPro: a browser-based platform for diallel crosses, mating designs, genetic parameters and prediction in plant and animal breeding"
abstract: >-
  BreedingPro is a self-contained web application for the analysis of plant and animal
  breeding experiments entirely in the browser, with no installation and no server-side
  computation. It plans crosses and field trials, recognises the mating and field design of
  a data table, analyses the trial, and estimates combining ability with the four Griffing
  methods, Hayman-Jinks and Gardner-Eberhart diallel analyses, North Carolina designs, triple
  test crosses, line x tester and partial diallels, generation means and variances with
  scaling tests, heritability with exact confidence intervals, correlations, path analysis
  and selection indices, genotype x environment interaction and stability (regression,
  AMMI, GGE biplot, two-stage REML), animal and sire models with BLUP and REML, Dickerson
  crossbreeding parameters, genomic prediction with GBLUP and the prediction of untested
  hybrids. It ends in editable publication-quality figures and a report with the methods
  written from the settings actually used and their references.
